Package: oneplus-erhai-bluetooth
Version: 2.3
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Depends: bluez
Description: Bluetooth support package for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 Since 2.2 this package no longer ships per-device address machinery. The
 shared DTB address (C0:FF:EE:13:1E:1A) is used for all devices; BT comes up
 instantly via stock bluetooth.service. The former erhai-bt-addr /
 erhai-bt-up services and scripts are retired by the postinst.
 .
 Since 2.3 the postinst also sets "FilterDiscoverable = false" in
 /etc/bluetooth/main.conf: BlueZ 5.85 defaults to hiding non-discoverable LE
 advertisers, which made the OnePlus Stylo pen invisible to bluetoothctl
 (its advertisement carries Flags=0x04, i.e. no LE-discoverable bit).
